{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01VCWnQWGRtp5uix6frcr9ad","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-user productivity + R&D control system. Grounded claims, drawn from `CLAUDE.md` and the project docs:\n\n**Purpose**\n- A personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that lives entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) â€” no syncing, no siblings, plain-text markdown as the single source of truth.\n\n**What it does (task management)**\n- Manages tasks across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) through a full lifecycle: Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, plus a quick-capture inbox and weekly reviews.\n- Stores everything as human-readable markdown (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`), so it stays accessible from any CLI or editor.\n\n**What it ships**\n- `anchor_gui.py` â€” the primary interface: a stdlib-only Python web server running persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`, generating an interactive dashboard that reads/writes the markdown directly.\n- `anchor.py` â€” a CLI engine mirroring the same logic (done/add/capture/cancel/save/restore) and generating a static `dashboard.html`.\n- `anchor_healthcheck.py` â€” a daily 5 AM self-test (via Task Scheduler) that parses all files, exercises every endpoint and task state on a throwaway port, walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed, and writes a dated health report.\n\n**The R&D control surface (its largest subsystem)**\n- Turns each project into a \"cockpit\" for the **trio** workflow â€” researchPrime (research) â†’ Crucible (planning) â†’ Foreman (build) â€” surfacing the most-recent session per lane with an honest status light.\n- Built in four design iterations, all merged to master: v2 (sessions/cached summaries/grass-catcher ideas/interactive terminal), v3 \"Mission Control\" (real ConPTY terminals via the one permitted native dep `pywinpty`, per-session git-worktree isolation, stacking window manager, Ghost World Labs branding), and v4 \"Project Cockpit\" (one seeded terminal substrate that loads a lane's skill once, engine toggle claudeâ†”gemini, inline expanding panels, cost/tokens/time rollup, deliverable launch-by-type).\n- Branded as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢.\"\n\n**Hard constraints**\n- Python stdlib only, with exactly one declared exception (`pywinpty`, lazy, terminal-only); enforced by an import scan in `distro.py`. Must run on any machine with Python 3.8+."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4420,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ca3f1bb-9c22-4b55-9b75-4e24a85a996b","uuid":"31c466a1-fb33-48fc-a944-9b39dcbf6009","request_id":"req_011Cc1YtpAearFocUUKpyFrr"}
